# Docs & rules ownership (mandatory)

Two documentation surfaces, **one owner per topic**. Never state the same rule twice — a duplicated rule drifts. Backend twin: `monolith/.cursor/rules/docs-pakem.mdc`.

| Surface | Owns | Shape |
|---------|------|-------|
| `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Normative pakem for agents: imperative must/never, exact paths, commands, gates | Self-sufficient — readable without opening any doc |
| `docs/**/*.md` | Human brief: what it is, where it lives, why | One paragraph + pointer table |
| `AGENTS.md` (repo root) | Pakem map: scope tag + one line per rule file | ~50 lines, zero rule detail |

## Human brief template (all four parts, nothing else)

1. `# Title` + one sentence naming the scope.
2. One paragraph: what it is, where the code lives, why it exists.
3. Pointer table: Code · Config · Backend contract · Tests · Pakem · Deep dive.
4. Nothing else — no history, no status dump, no restated rules.

## Doc kinds and size budgets (enforced by `scripts/check-docs.mjs`)

Not every living doc is a brief. The kind comes from the file name, so a new kind is a deliberate choice:

| Kind | File | Max lines |
|------|------|-----------|
| Index | `docs/README.md` | 150 |
| Brief | anything else, including every `README.md` under a subdirectory | 90 |
| Deep dive | `reference.md`, `reference-*.md` | 400 |
| Tracker | `implementation-status.md` | 500 |
| Glossary | `naming-conventions.md` | 200 |
| Edge case | `*-edge-cases.md`, `daily-free-trial.md` | 200 |

- A **deep dive** must be linked from the `README.md` in the same directory. Unlinked, it is a second front door to the same topic.
- Over budget means the content belongs in a rule file or in the Monolith `docs/archive/`. The allowlist `docs/.docs-budget-allowlist.json` is the last resort, every entry carries a reason, and an entry whose file now fits is itself a finding.
- Glob-scoped rule ≤ 60 lines; all always-on rules combined ≤ 150. The always-on budget is the context every conversation pays for; when it is exceeded, a rule that only matters for one area must move to a glob scope.

## Placement

- One file per concern under `docs/`, one row in [docs/README.md](../../docs/README.md). A SPA brief that needs schema or API detail gets a `reference.md` next to it (or `reference-<topic>.md` when one file would outgrow the budget), linked from the brief.
- **Never** create `docs/agents/` — agent rules live in `.cursor/rules/`.
- Contract changes (API shapes, headers, cookies/CSRF, route names) update both this tree and `monolith/docs/integration/vue-workers-spa.md`.
- English only, in both surfaces.

## Keeping it true

- Behavior change in the same task/PR: update the owning brief, and the rule file when an invariant moved.
- Keyword **`wrap up the docs`** = session-wide consolidation of code ↔ docs ↔ rules across both repos, then run the gates.
- Gates: `npm run check:docs`, `npm run check:i18n`, `npm run type-check`, `npm test`; backend `php artisan test --filter=Documentation` when a Monolith doc moved.
